WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.379 --> 00:00:07.330
Hi, I'm Allison Powell and I am an actor/
filmmaker. And today I'm going to be talking

00:00:07.330 --> 00:00:10.840
to you about one of the hardest lessons
that I had to learn when I was starting

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:16.570
out as a filmmaker as a producer and
that is something that I'm still working

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:23.320
on in my daily life and it is the
ability to admit that you don't know how

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:28.539
to do something and being vulnerable
enough and confident enough to ask for

00:00:28.539 --> 00:00:34.510
help so I always tell people now my
three favorite word's on a film set

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:41.140
are I don't know and those three words
can actually be incredibly hard to say

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:44.859
especially when you're just starting out
and you want people to think that you've

00:00:44.859 --> 00:00:48.639
got this you're smart you're confident
you know what you're doing they can

00:00:48.639 --> 00:00:53.109
trust you they definitely should have
hired you you're dependable but in

00:00:53.109 --> 00:00:58.600
reality not everyone on a set can know
everything you can't know how to do

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:05.770
everything like that would just be
insane and so I started out pretending

00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:10.450
that I knew what something meant or what
a piece of equipment was or I'd go away

00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:16.000
for ten minutes and maybe try to do
whatever they asked me to do or what I

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:20.289
thought they asked me to do and then I
would come back and just say yeah it's

00:01:20.289 --> 00:01:25.960
not working or I couldn't find it or I
can't figure it out and for some reason

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:31.210
I thought it was better to kind of lie
in these situations rather than just

00:01:31.210 --> 00:01:34.810
being upfront and saying I don't know
what that is or I don't know how to do

00:01:34.810 --> 00:01:40.750
that or I don't know who that is and
just asking for help it's a really

00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:44.380
really difficult thing to do that I
don't think a lot of people realize and

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:48.340
not enough people talk about it takes
actually an incredible amount of

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:53.679
confidence to admit to someone that you
don't know something and and or that you

00:01:53.679 --> 00:01:59.590
need help and I think it's a really
important skill set for new filmmakers

00:01:59.590 --> 00:02:04.149
to learn and to embrace because the only
way that you're going to learn how to do

00:02:04.149 --> 00:02:10.119
something is by admitting that you don't
already know how to do it so now I do

00:02:10.119 --> 00:02:15.340
that on almost every film set I'm on and
I try to do it more in my day

00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:20.110
life as well so for example we were
doing some pickup shots for my feature

00:02:20.110 --> 00:02:26.200
and they were driving so the DP built a
whole camera rig on top of a car he

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:30.190
brought you at everything in plays with
ratchet straps and then at the end of

00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:33.970
the day when we were breaking stuff down
and I was helping out with that I just

00:02:33.970 --> 00:02:38.680
said to the AC who was working next to
me I said I don't know how to take off

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:43.090
ratchet straps so I'm gonna watch you do
it and then you're gonna watch me do it

00:02:43.090 --> 00:02:47.739
and then I'll know how and what was so
funny is he turned to me and he said I

00:02:47.739 --> 00:02:53.250
don't know how to take off ratchet
straps either and I had just assumed

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:59.019
because he seemed have more experience
in the camera department than me maybe

00:02:59.019 --> 00:03:02.650
because he was a guy I just assumed that
he would know how to do it and what was

00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:06.459
great is he just admitted right to me
that he didn't know how to do it either

00:03:06.459 --> 00:03:12.250
so both of us had to go to the DP and
say hey we don't really know how to do

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:15.220
this
one of the first shorts that I was on as

00:03:15.220 --> 00:03:19.269
a producer and part of a producing team
I said to the producer who was filling

00:03:19.269 --> 00:03:23.889
in all of the sag paperwork for us I
said can i watch you fill it out and I

00:03:23.889 --> 00:03:28.810
just stood looking over her shoulder as
she filled in everything and she went to

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:31.930
the actors and have them fill out their
contracts because I didn't know how to

00:03:31.930 --> 00:03:38.109
do it and I wanted to learn the only way
that you will learn is by asking for

00:03:38.109 --> 00:03:41.620
help and admitting that you don't know
how to do something and I want you to

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:47.680
really embrace these words I don't know
when you're on set embrace your

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:52.810
vulnerability as a filmmaker I think
people think and I certainly used to

00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:56.500
think that it was a sign of weakness to
admit that you didn't know how to do

00:03:56.500 --> 00:04:01.090
something and people would fire me they
would think I didn't belong they would

00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:07.239
not ask me to do anything in the future
and the total opposite happens people

00:04:07.239 --> 00:04:11.980
get more excited they want to teach you
they want to help you they want you to

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:16.299
expand your knowledge base so that then
the next time they ask you or the next

00:04:16.299 --> 00:04:20.289
time they want to hire you for a project
you already know the shorthand you know

00:04:20.289 --> 00:04:25.539
what they're asking you to do when you
embrace that vulnerability you also make

00:04:25.539 --> 00:04:30.259
people want to work with you if you just
Marche around acting like you know

00:04:30.259 --> 00:04:35.689
everything and know how to do everything
people don't like that it's gonna be

00:04:35.689 --> 00:04:41.389
arrogant it's gonna turn people off if
instead you ask for help or offer help

00:04:41.389 --> 00:04:46.789
when it's needed people are going to
want to be around that type of energy so

00:04:46.789 --> 00:04:53.029
being vulnerable is a great way to get
people on your side and I say being

00:04:53.029 --> 00:04:57.080
vulnerable but it's really being
confident it's really having the

00:04:57.080 --> 00:05:02.539
confidence to be vulnerable and say I
don't know those are the three best

00:05:02.539 --> 00:05:07.400
words on a film set it also is really
important to remember that that could be

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:11.210
a safety concern if you don't know how
to do something or don't know what a

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:16.699
piece of equipment is or how to use it
you need to say that you will not get in

00:05:16.699 --> 00:05:20.539
trouble you will get in trouble if you
pretend that you know how to do it and

00:05:20.539 --> 00:05:26.449
somebody gets injured or something gets
broken or a lot of time is lost and so

00:05:26.449 --> 00:05:30.830
again it's just better to have that
confidence to be vulnerable upfront and

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:35.750
say you don't know how to do something
and then either learn or observe so that

00:05:35.750 --> 00:05:41.029
the next time you can do it but onset is
not the place to pretend that you know

00:05:41.029 --> 00:05:45.139
everything pretend that you tried to go
and do something to come back and lie

00:05:45.139 --> 00:05:50.089
about it which is what I definitely used
to do it's the place to say hey I don't

00:05:50.089 --> 00:05:54.199
know how to do this but I'm here to
learn and I'm willing to learn and I

00:05:54.199 --> 00:05:59.199
want you to show me so that I know how
to do it tomorrow or on the next project

00:05:59.199 --> 00:06:03.589
and that is my secret weapon as a
filmmaker

00:06:03.589 --> 00:06:09.169
it's how I learned everything I know
pretty much is by having the confidence

00:06:09.169 --> 00:06:15.020
to be vulnerable and go up to someone
and say I don't know how to do that can

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:20.389
i watch you can you show me can you talk
me through it so if you want to become a

00:06:20.389 --> 00:06:26.300
better filmmaker have the confidence to
be vulnerable ask for help and admit you

00:06:26.300 --> 00:06:31.449
don't know thanks for watching

